endered-description=3D"" data-track-load=3D"description_content"><p>Given a=
n integer <code>n</code>, return <em>an array </em><code>ans</code><em> of =
length </em><code>n + 1</code><em> such that for each </em><code>i</code><e=
m> </em>(<code>0 &lt;=3D i &lt;=3D n</code>)<em>, </em><code>ans[i]</code><=
em> is the <strong>number of </strong></em><code>1</code><em><strong>'s</st=
rong> in the binary representation of </em><code>i</code>.</p>
Do not solve it with built-in functions (i.e., like <code>__builtin_popcoun=
t</code> in C++).
<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 1:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n =3D 2
<strong>Output:</strong> [0,1,1]
<strong>Explanation:</strong>
0 --&gt; 0
1 --&gt; 1
2 --&gt; 10
</pre>

<p><strong class=3D"example">Example 2:</strong></p>

<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n =3D 5
<strong>Output:</strong> [0,1,1,2,1,2]
<strong>Explanation:</strong>
0 --&gt; 0
1 --&gt; 1
2 --&gt; 10
3 --&gt; 11
4 --&gt; 100
5 --&gt; 101
</pre>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li><code>0 &lt;=3D n &lt;=3D 10<sup>5</sup></code></li>
</ul>

<p>&nbsp;</p>
<p><strong>Follow up:</strong></p>

<ul>
	<li>It is very easy to come up with a solution with a runtime of <code>O(n=
 log n)</code>. Can you do it in linear time <code>O(n)</code> and possibly=
 in a single pass?</li>
</ul>
